{"name":"Delicate Frost","hex":"#c5ead3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost","wikidata":"Q4590598"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg/500px-Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg/1280px-Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en